  "id": "20dee190-43ab-5c9c-aa4c-ddf373d72460",
  "slug": "pizza-sauce-and-dough",
  "name": "Pizza Sauce and Dough",
  "recipe_type": "side",
  "brief_description": "The basic pizza dough and sauce ready and waiting for your favorite toppings! This recipe makes 2 pizzas; either make both, or freeze one.",
  "cuisine": null,
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "In a small bowl, dissolve yeast and sugar in warm water. Let stand until creamy, about 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "In a food processor, combine flour, Italian seasoning and salt. Pulse until mixed. Add yeast mixture, flat beer and oil. Pulse until a ball is formed. Scrape dough out onto a lightly floured surface, and knead for several minutes until dough is smooth and elastic. Allow dough to rest for 2 to 3 minutes. Divide dough in half, and shape into balls. Place dough balls in separate bowls, and cover with plastic wrap. Allow to rise at room temperature for about 1 hour, then store in the refrigerate overnight."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "To make the sauce: Heat olive oil in a saucepan over medium heat. Saute onions until tender. Stir in garlic, and cook for 1 minute. Crush tomatoes into saucepan. Add tomato paste, basil, parsley and oregano. Simmer for 10 minutes."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 20,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 40,
